Design of per-fixture ledger:
```
def stage_calls(sb, target):
    g = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(sb/GATE), "--json", str(target)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
    try: gd = json.loads(g.stdout)
    except: gd = {"verdict": f"crash(exit{g.returncode})"}
    s = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(sb/AUD), str(target)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
    try: sd = json.loads(s.stdout)
    except: sd = {"verdict":"?", "failed_rules":[]}
    return gd, sd
```
Targets must be sandbox paths (the instruments run with sandbox root; they don't need ROOT except spec default — auditor's DEFAULT_SPEC is relative to its own location in the sandbox → sandbox rule_spec. Good.)

For canonical targets use the sandbox schemas.

